essageTitle":"Add Javadoc comments to public classes and methods","messageBody":"Coverage was at 23% (13/57 public elements), below the level\u0027s 50%\nminimum. Add class-level and method-level Javadoc across Kiki, Ui,\nParser, Storage, TaskList, Task, ToDos, Deadlines, Events, and\nKikiException, raising coverage to 73%. The remaining gaps are all\ntrivial one-line getters and toString() overrides, which the coding\nstandard explicitly exempts from requiring Javadoc.\n","tags":["A-JavaDoc"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":186,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"65bb01100d9ac1ba551852486b481ba1727a0a05","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Remove extraneous blank lines flagged by coding standard","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":0,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"d26b02013ba91d2ddf45afb0a50182c4e81fdb42","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add seedu-java-coding-standard skill and mandate it","messageBody":"This project needs to follow the SE-EDU intermediate Java coding\nstandard for all code going forward. Add a project-specific skill\nencoding its naming, layout, statement, and comment rules, and\nreference it from AGENTS.md so it\u0027s invoked on every .java edit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":102,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"35cad733c737841ca94f55eb7cb762e557da72de","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add seedu-git-standard skill and mandate it","messageBody":"Same reasoning as the Java coding standard: encode the SE-EDU Git\nconventions (commit subject/body rules, branch naming) as a\nproject-specific skill, and reference it from AGENTS.md so it\u0027s\ninvoked whenever a commit message or branch name is drafted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n","tags":["A-CodingStandard"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":6